## 06:25 BST — S04 baseline FIX-2 (after user feedback on map composite)

**User feedback in Preview**: the McKechnie map composite I did at 01:08 had weirdly-placed site labels and the red coastal-spawn POLYGONS read as confusingly-labeled spots. Root cause: the McKechnie figure is a two-panel composition (left = HG detail with site triangles; right = NE Pacific regional context with red SPAWN-EXTENT POLYGONS along the BC mainland coast) — I composited a narrow horizontal STRIP that squished both panels together and cut off the bottom labels (785T/781T sites, scale bar), leaving the panel labels in geographically nonsensical positions.

**Fix applied (Option B from original audit — what the audit said was safer):**
- Backed up post-map-composite state to `_originals/04_baseline.png.premapfix.bak`
- Cleared the banner region (cols 136–3704 × rows 716–1406, 3568×690 px) to slide background (#FBFAF7 cream sampled from corner)
- Rendered hero line "Herring were 49% of all fish at 99% of sites across 10,700 years." in Georgia Bold 96px dark ink, centered horizontally and vertically
- Added a 240×4 px rust accent rule (#C4683E) below the hero text as a subtle anchor

The slide now reads: eyebrow → title → 5 stat cards → hero line + accent → bottom quote → source. Clean, no map, no weird labels.

`04_baseline.png` re-saved at 3840×2160, 233 KB.


